From 5b6f390af6a51ebc01f71fe34485980a214edad3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: webOS Phoenix <dev@webosphoenix.org>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 19:12:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Another of the account's devices' position (location sharing)

webOS Phoenix VMs in UTM on an iPad cannot reach the iPad's Core
Location, Wi-Fi or cells: the network handler only knows the town from
the IP address. The user's Phoenix account can carry the position of
another device they own (Safari on that iPad, a Shortcut, a phone with
GPS), which the account service gives as locationRelay.

- network: at each request, and with each 60 s update while one runs,
  ask luna://org.webosphoenix.service.account/locationRelay. A position
  in the reply is the network handler's answer (with its age, accuracy,
  altitude, heading and speed); while there is one (2.5 minutes after it
  last came) no Wi-Fi, cell or IP query is posted.
- network: with the "manual" provider, the answer waits for the account
  service (at most 3 s) and is its position if it has one, else the
  user's own.
- The reply carries no position when this device's switch (Settings) or
  the account's sharing is off, or none is fresh: the handler goes on as
  before.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [webOS Phoenix configuration]
